
/** \page "Getting Started"

!!! Getting Started

!!Aquiring PPR
PPR is a commercial product maintained and supported by PTV AG and is 
part of the navi-platform. Visit www.ptv.de for more information. 
Alternatively, the free Platinum C++ framework is available under the LGPL,
which is mostly identical to PPR.

!!Including PPR Headers
The header files are arranged in include directories named by the module
namespace. The ptv-io headers are therefore placed in <includedir>/ptv/io.
Library headers are always included with a path beginning at the top-level
namespace.

\code
#include <ptv/Api.h>
#include <ptv/io/IOStream.h>
\endcode

!!Linking against PPR
The libraries built from each module follow a special naming scheme which
is derived from the module namespace as shown in the following table.

||Namespace||Win32||Unix
|ptv|ptv.dll|libptv.so
|ptv::io|ptv-io.dll|libptv-io.so

!!Building PPR from source
The cross-platform build tool 'jam' is used to build PPR on all platforms
with a unified build system. To build PPR for your system run the jam tool
in the project root with some of the following parameters:

||Argument||Possible Value||Default Value
|CONFIG|debug / release|debug
|TOOLSET| vc7 / vc8 / gcc /qcc / evc4|---
|BYTEORDER| le / be|le

Jam executables for various platforms are provided in the jam subdirectory.
For example, to build PPR for windows with the VC7 compiler open the Visual 
Studio build shell and run:

@code
jam\jam.exe -sCONFIG=release -sTOOLSET=vc7
@endcode

Of course jam-enabled project files are provided for many IDE's too 
(Visual Studio, Eclipse, KDevelop...), as well as .bat and unix shell
scripts for convenience.

*/

